From: Rasheed <99349713+gitRasheed@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 23:34:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 15/61] dy.dx: stop early when eval.point is not supplied

The documented default eval.point = NULL always failed deep inside with
"undefined columns selected" (cbind() of the NULL point drops the
eval.point column). The docs say eval.point must be provided, so stop
up front with a clear message instead of defaulting to "overall".

Before -> after, dy.dx(rnorm(60), sin(x)):
  Error "undefined columns selected"
  -> Error "eval.point must be provided: numeric point(s) or 'overall'"
Numeric and "overall" calls are unchanged (eval.point = 0.5: 0.5236 /
0.00796; "overall": 0.6656).
---
 R/dy_dx.R | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/R/dy_dx.R b/R/dy_dx.R
index 2f557b8..10d6429 100644
--- a/R/dy_dx.R
+++ b/R/dy_dx.R
@@ -29,6 +29,9 @@
 #' @export
 
 dy.dx <- function(x, y, eval.point = NULL){
+  
+  if(is.null(eval.point) || length(eval.point) == 0)
+    stop("eval.point must be provided: numeric point(s) or 'overall'")
 
   if(any(class(x)%in%c("tbl","data.table"))) x <- as.vector(unlist(x))
   if(any(class(y)%in%c("tbl","data.table"))) y <- as.vector(unlist(y))
